### Decision LOCKED — Figma html.to.design import (2026-09-10)
**Problem:** html.to.design drops CSS `background-image` and often leaves empty `Image (...)` frames when `src` 404s (GitHub Pages before merge, remote cfbhall.com WebP, or `file://`).

**Rules (do not regress):**
1. Heroes + card photos = **`<img>` tags** with `width`/`height`; photo + shade **position:absolute** overlay; copy in flex column (`justify-content: flex-end`) — **not** `background-image` or in-flow img height
2. Live pages + JSON: local JPEGs in `assets/images/happenings/` (`hero-listing.jpg`, `hero-ticketed.jpg`, `hero-exhibit.jpg`); `happenings.js` sets hero `img.src` from `ev.image`
3. **Import capture = localhost only:** `python3 -m http.server 8080` from repo root; never `file://`
4. Import URLs use **absolute** `http://127.0.0.1:8080/...` so the plugin can fetch images:
   - **Listing (validated):** `http://127.0.0.1:8080/happenings-listing-import.html`
   - **Full flow:** `screens/01-listing-d.html` … `09-related-m.html` — see `screens/index.html`
5. Regenerate after edits: `python3 scripts/generate_figma_import.py` && `python3 screens/generate_screens.py`
6. Figma target: **Wireframes 2** userflow [553:1219](https://www.figma.com/design/jcbtHK67Ih9BsBxFQK7F7l/College-Football---Global-Banner?node-id=553-1219) — Matt imports via html.to.design plugin (not MCP capture)
7. Empty card images in Figma = broken src at capture time → re-import from localhost, do not patch with MCP upload

